WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.984
The remaining targets
all follow one pattern:

2
00:00:02.984 --> 00:00:07.925
find the tool that already owns the setting,
and let Ansible do only what's left.

3
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:10.889
On VMware, the virtual
machines can go to Arc,

4
00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:15.912
while the hypervisor and appliances,
which can't run an agent, are Ansible's.

5
00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:18.916
On Infoblox, Ansible
works through the A P I,

6
00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:22.350
with an account scoped to
the objects it manages.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.959
On a Windows server under Arc,
the operating system belongs

8
00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:29.788
to machine configuration, but
the application can be Ansible's.

9
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:33.012
And in the cloud, the
provider's inventory is for

10
00:00:33.012 --> 00:00:35.988
checking against the C
M D B, not replacing it.

11
00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:37.900
Next, running the platform.
